"html": "\n<section class=\"section service-editorial\"><div class=\"shell service-reading\"><nav class=\"service-jump-links\" aria-label=\"On this service page\"><a href=\"#service-work\">Services</a><a href=\"#service-method\">Repair &amp; installation</a><a href=\"#service-quote\">Costs &amp; quote</a><a href=\"#service-faq\">FAQs</a><a href=\"#service-booking\">Book a visit</a></nav><aside class=\"service-answer\" data-service-answer><h2>What to do next</h2><p>A running cistern or failed flush is different from wastewater backing up through the toilet. Tell us whether water runs into the bowl, leaks outside the fitting or rises when flushed. Avoid affected fixtures if wastewater is returning and keep clear of it. Our plumber assesses the fixture and drainage involved, then explains compatible parts, repairs and any separate clearing work in the written quote. You can request a visit without diagnosing the fault.</p><p><a href=\"insights-reporting-a-plumbing-leak.html\">Record water symptoms without dismantling fixtures</a>. <a href=\"contact.html?service=toilet-repairs-perth.html\">Request an assessment and written quote</a>.</p></aside><div id=\"service-work\" class=\"service-editorial-part\"><h2>Toilet and cistern repair services</h2><h3>A running cistern or water that will not stop</h3><p>A toilet that continues running after a flush needs the cistern components and relevant connections assessed. We identify the part of the fixture involved and whether compatible replacement parts are suitable. Tell us whether water is running into the bowl, leaking outside the toilet or affecting the surrounding floor.</p>\n<h3>Slow filling, weak flushing and controls that fail</h3><p>Filling and flushing problems are not all the same repair. We assess the toilet type, controls, accessible supply connection and reported behaviour before setting the scope. A concealed cistern may need a different access plan from an exposed one; any access work is discussed before it is assumed in the quote.</p>\n<h3>Blocked toilets and overflow</h3><p>When waste will not clear or the bowl rises during use, we assess whether the problem is at the fixture or in the drainage serving it. Other affected drains are useful information for the visit. If several fixtures back up, our <a href=\"blocked-drains-perth.html\">blocked-drain clearing service</a> covers the wider drainage scope.</p><figure class=\"service-editorial-figure\"><img srcset=\"hot-water-drainage-perth-480.webp 480w, hot-water-drainage-perth-960.webp 960w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 540px) calc(100vw - 48px), 480px\" loading=\"lazy\"\n            class=\"service-editorial-image\"\n            src=\"hot-water-drainage-perth.png\"\n            width=\"1672\"\n            height=\"941\"\n            alt=\"Plumbing service illustration showing drain access beside hot-water equipment\"\n\n          /></figure></div>\n<div id=\"service-method\" class=\"service-editorial-part\"><h2>How we assess and complete a toilet repair</h2><p>Our plumber checks the reported fault, the fixture condition and the components that can be safely accessed. We explain whether the proposed work concerns the flush mechanism, filling components, connections or drainage. That distinction helps avoid approving a fixture replacement when the actual request is a component repair or a blocked drain.</p>\n<h3>Component repair or a replacement toilet</h3><p>The condition of the toilet, compatible parts and access influence the options. A replacement toilet needs its installation requirements assessed separately; connection positions and fixture dimensions matter. We discuss the parts or fixture to be supplied and any additional connection work before you approve the written quote.</p>\n<p>For the agreed work, we check the relevant filling, flushing or repaired connection and explain the outcome. If water around the toilet comes from an unclear source, we discuss a separate <a href=\"water-leak-detection-perth.html\">leak investigation</a> rather than treating every wet floor as a cistern fault. Rental jobs also need the approval contact and arrangements for access to the bathroom.</p></div><p class=\"service-trade-note\">Our Perth plumbing and electrical work is carried out by appropriately licensed trades. Licence details are available on request.</p><p class=\"service-safety\"><strong>Safety:</strong> Avoid contact with wastewater and keep people away from an overflowing toilet. Do not continue using an affected fixture if it is backing up. For immediate danger, Call 000.</p><!-- keyword-gap:start --><div class=\"keyword-gap-content\" data-keyword-gap><div class=\"keyword-gap-part\" id=\"gap-toilet-repair-or-installation\"><h2>Choose between toilet repair, installation and drain clearing</h2><p>Start with the task rather than ordering a new suite for every fault. A running cistern or unreliable flush belongs with this repair assessment. A proposed complete replacement needs its product and connection requirements checked. Water backing up in the bowl belongs with drainage assessment.</p><p>If you are comparing replacement options, include the selected product, dimensions if available and who supplies it. Ask the quote to identify removal, connection changes and any separate floor or wall work. The existing toilet-repair guide price is not a complete installed-suite package.</p><ul class=\"intent-links\"><li><a href=\"fixtures-appliances-perth.html#gap-toilet-installation\">Toilet installation and replacement enquiries</a></li><li><a href=\"blocked-drains-perth.html#gap-blocked-toilet-shower\">Blocked toilets and shower drains</a></li><li><a href=\"contact.html?service=toilet-repairs-perth.html\">Arrange assessment of a toilet or cistern fault</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"keyword-gap-part\" id=\"learn-about-toilet-repairs-perth\"><h2>Toilet repairs Perth: symptoms and service choices</h2><h3>Running cisterns and water at the toilet base</h3><p>A running toilet may continue filling or passing water through the cistern and pan. Water at the base may involve a connection, fixture or another source. These observations need different checks and do not establish that the whole suite must be replaced.</p><h3>A toilet cistern that refills on its own</h3><p>Water may be escaping from the cistern so the fill mechanism runs again, but the components need inspection. Describe the timing and visible water. A parts repair may be appropriate; a new suite is not the automatic next step.</p><ul class=\"intent-links\"><li><a href=\"blocked-drains-perth.html\">When the symptom belongs with drainage</a></li></ul></div></div><!-- keyword-gap:end --></div></section>" as TrustedHtml
},
